## 10. Checklist: Manager Pre-Joining to Day 90

Print this and track your progress:

### Pre-Joining (1–2 weeks before)
- [ ] Submit hardware and software requests to IT
- [ ] Send warm welcome email to new hire
- [ ] Confirm receipt and answer any questions
- [ ] Assign a buddy and brief them
- [ ] Announce new hire to team
- [ ] Draft 30-day onboarding plan
- [ ] Coordinate with HR on admin items
- [ ] Prepare first-day materials (handbook, org chart, map)

### Day 1
- [ ] Greet new hire with enthusiasm
- [ ] Complete 30–45 min first meeting covering role, expectations, logistics
- [ ] Introduce to team and buddy
- [ ] End-of-day check-in at 5 p.m.

### Week 1
- [ ] Daily 5–10 min check-ins
- [ ] Introduce to 5+ key people
- [ ] Have them shadow 1 meeting or call
- [ ] Clarify 30-day goals in writing
- [ ] Friday: Reflect on how they're settling in

### Weeks 2–4 (Days 8–30)
- [ ] Weekly 1:1 meetings (min. 30 min)
- [ ] Assign and review first small task
- [ ] Identify 2–3 must-know SOPs; have them read and summarize
- [ ] Cross-functional coffee chats (4–5 people)
- [ ] Day 30: Document observations for 30-day review
- [ ] Day 30: Formalize feedback and discuss progress

### Weeks 5–8 (Days 31–60)
- [ ] Continue weekly 1:1s
- [ ] Assign medium-complexity tasks
- [ ] Encourage proactive problem-solving
- [ ] Day 50–60: Mid-point check-in
- [ ] Discuss development goals for Days 60–90

### Weeks 9–13 (Days 61–90)
- [ ] Continue weekly 1:1s
- [ ] Assign meaningful project/workstream for them to own
- [ ] Observe demonstration of company values
- [ ] Day 90: Conduct formal probation review with HR
- [ ] Decision: Confirm permanent employment, extend probation, or separate
- [ ] Finalize 6-month development plan

